        "text_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "vince.wolff@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "vince.wolff@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 15 2019 17:34:36 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">ADAPT for Gamma3</span></span><br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 15 2019 17:48:50 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "largeheadline_copy_1": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "jeannie.chan@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "vince.wolff@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Fri Feb 23 2018 11:50:11 GMT-0500",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "line2": "<p>Integrated seamlessly into the surgeon’s workflow, the ADAPT system, can potentially reduce radiation exposure and operative time.&nbsp; Studies have shown that orthopaedic surgeons are 5.39x more likely to have cancer compared to other healthcare workers.<sup>1</sup> ADAPT for Gamma3 has shown to reduce radiation exposure by 11%<sup>2</sup>, and reduce OR time by 9%.<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n<p>Half of the total radiation time for nailing procedures occurs during freehand distal locking.<sup>,3,4</sup>ADAPT supports distal locking using the Gamma Distal Targeting system and has been shown to distally lock up to 2 screws with a median of 5 shots.<sup>5</sup></p>\r\n<p>Want more information about this system? Learn more about ADAPT here.&nbsp;</p>\r\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 15 2019 17:49:02 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/largeheadline",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,1)",
          "textIsRich": [
            "true",
            "true"
          ]
        },
